PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 1 shows sharp consolidation on B (8 votes) vs. D (3) and lingering C/D uncertainty (1). B praised for simultaneously meeting all 4 criteria: sole Alex/Tyler directors + equal voting shares for control; Class A (voting, no dividends) enabling Alex salary-only; Class B (voting, dividends) for Tyler; pre-authorized Class C (non-voting + liquidation rights) usable for passive investors. Drafting typo in B ("voting rights" for Class B) universally treated as "dividends" without altering fit. 

D still defended for simplicity/equal control/salary flexibility via employment agreement, with OBCA s.168 amendment route for future non-voting class; critics say this violates "authorized" language in req. 4. C fails because its Class C has zero economic rights (unattractive/unusable for investors). A/D give both founders identical dividend rights (no payout separation). E adds Tyler's sons as directors (breaks equal control). 

Unresolved issues preserved: whether post-incorp amendment satisfies req. 4; whether non-voting shares must carry economic rights to attract investors. Prior view updated—B now clearly strongest; none other fully clean.}

